    "result": "Perfect! The bug has been successfully fixed. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Problem**: `frai gate init --ci` did not create the GitHub Actions workflow file (`.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`), even though the same command works correctly when run directly with `frai-gate`.\n\n**Root Cause**: The `--ci` flag was defined on the main `frai` program (line 605), so commander.js consumed it at the top level instead of passing it to the `gate` subcommand. The gate command's action handler only received `['init']` instead of `['init', '--ci']`.\n\n**Solution**: Modified the `gate` command's action handler to:\n1. Accept the `command` parameter from commander.js\n2. Access the parent command's parsed options using `command.parent?.opts()`\n3. Check if `--ci` is set in the parent options and add it to the arguments passed to frai-gate\n\n**Files Changed**:\n- `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` - Updated the gate command handler to pass through the `--ci` flag\n- `packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js` - Rebuilt with the fix\n\n**Verification**: \n\u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both FRAI-SPEC.md and .github/workflows/rai-gate.yml  \n\u2705 `frai gate init` (without --ci) still works correctly, creating only FRAI-SPEC.md",
